# =============================================================================
# .trivyignore — reviewed Trivy exceptions
# =============================================================================
# Findings listed here are suppressed in BOTH Trivy scans:
#   * .github/workflows/server-ci.yml — server/Dockerfile image (blocks merges)
#   * .github/workflows/trivy.yml     — repository filesystem
#
# An upgrade is always preferred. Add an entry only for a false positive, or for
# a vulnerability that is not exploitable in AirFlex and cannot be upgraded yet.
# Findings without an available fix do not need an entry: the scans skip them.
#
# Every entry needs a comment with the affected package, the reason, who
# approved it and a tracking issue, plus an expiry date after which Trivy
# reports the finding again:
#
#   # <package> — <why this is safe to ignore>
#   # Approved by: <GitHub login>   Tracking: #<issue>
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# There are currently no approved exceptions.
